          "type": "turn",
          "question": "my poo has been really dark, almost black and sticky, for three days and I feel light headed when i stand",
          "answer": "The symptoms of dark, sticky stool and lightheadedness are categorized as **routine** urgency. This means while there are no immediate red flags for emergency care based on standard patterns, the situation still requires attention. If symptoms worsen or new symptoms develop, it is important to seek medical advice.\n\nDark, sticky stools can indicate gastrointestinal bleeding, which is often digested blood. This type of presentation could be serious and warrants medical evaluation to rule out conditions like ulcers or other causes of bleeding in the digestive tract. Lightheadedness, especially when standing, might be related to other systemic issues, such as dehydration or anemia, but it can also be associated with the gastrointestinal symptoms.\n\nGiven your specific symptoms, a healthcare provider might explore several potential issues such as iron-deficiency anemia, gastrointestinal diseases including gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD), or other possibilities.\n\nIt's important to discuss these symptoms with a clinician who can properly assess them in context and recommend further evaluation or treatment based on your overall health.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
